# Session open

When this Cursor Local session opens, run the startup contract in
`docs/ops/ai/CURSOR-RULES.md`, then immediately continue Session lifecycle
phase 2 (continuous assigned-queue pass) in the **same turn**.

Run `~/.cursor/lgfc-wake-ctl.sh startup --session <this chat uuid>`. Do not
rebind. Do not stop another session's loop. Do not start a second loop.

## Hard distinctions (do not re-litigate)

- Wake loop + runner = connectivity keepalives for this chat.
- Continuous workflow = the agent's job: read the GitHub queue and move
  eligible Issues without waiting for a tick.
- Startup = orientation only. It authorizes no Issue, pull request, or
  file edit.
- Ending startup is not a stop. Do not wait for the next tick. Do not go
  idle because the loop is stopped — continue the open-Issue pass; if this
  chat is the recorded owner and nothing can move, start exactly one loop
  and report its PID (#5012).

An unapproved Cursor workaround is denied. Where this card disagrees with
`docs/governance/AGENT-EXECUTION.md`, that document wins.
